<td id="tab2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td">
<span id="tab2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="tab2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="tab2.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tianyu Ruan</span>  is a PhD candidate in Operations Research and Cybernetics at the Academy of Mathematics and Systems Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences. His research interests include deep learning theory and geometry-inspired machine learning methods.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="tab3" class="ltx_float biography">
<table id="tab3.1" class="ltx_tabular">
<tr id="tab3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="tab3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td"><img src="2510.02520v1/Author_photos/ChihaoZhang.jpg" id="g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:86/125;" width="86" height="125" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td>
<td id="tab3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td">
<span id="tab3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="tab3.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="tab3.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Chihao Zhang</span>  is an Assistant Professor with the Academy of Mathematics and Systems Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences.
His research interests include machine learning, data mining, pattern recognition and bioinformatics.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="tab4" class="ltx_float biography">
<table id="tab4.1" class="ltx_tabular">
<tr id="tab4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="tab4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td"><img src="2510.02520v1/Author_photos/ShihuaZhang.jpg" id="g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:88/125;" width="88" height="125" alt="[Uncaptioned image]"></td>
<td id="tab4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td">
<span id="tab4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="tab4.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="tab4.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shihua Zhang</span>  received the Ph.D. degree in applied mathematics and bioinformatics from the Academy of Mathematics and Systems Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences in 2008 with the highest honor. He joined the same institute as an Assistant Professor in 2008 and is currently Professor. His research interests are mainly in bioinformatics and computational biology, data mining, machine learning, and deep learning. He has won various awards and honors including the National High-level Talent Program Leading Talents (2022) and Top-notch Talents (2018), NSFC for Excellent Young Scholars (2014), Outstanding Young Scientist Program of CAS (2014), and Youth Science and Technology Award of China (2013). Now he serves as a Section Editor of PLOS Computational Biology.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Key Properties of Stiefel Manifold <math id="A1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce the fundamental properties of <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{A\in M_{n\times k}:A^{T}\cdot A=I_{k\times k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{A\in M_{n\times k}:A^{T}\cdot A=I_{k\times k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> as a Riemannian manifold (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Edelman et al. [29]</a></cite> for more information). These properties provide insights into how to study vector fields on the Stiefel manifold and compute geodesics.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmProperty1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmProperty1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 1</span></span><span id="ThmProperty1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tangent space of <math id="ThmProperty1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="ThmProperty1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmProperty1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmProperty1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="ThmProperty1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=YA+(1-YY^{T})B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=YA+(1-YY^{T})B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="ThmProperty1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where <math id="ThmProperty1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="ThmProperty1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a skew-symmetric matrix and <math id="ThmProperty1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary <math id="ThmProperty1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times k</annotation></semantics></math> matrix.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span>: Suppose <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a differentiable curve of <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)=Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)=Y</annotation></semantics></math>. We have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\cdot\gamma(t)=I_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\cdot\gamma(t)=I_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Take the derivative of both sides of the equation, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\cdot\dot{\gamma}(t)+\dot{\gamma}^{T}(t)\cdot\gamma(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\cdot\dot{\gamma}(t)+\dot{\gamma}^{T}(t)\cdot\gamma(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\gamma}(t)^{T}Y+Y^{T}\dot{\gamma}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\gamma}(t)^{T}Y+Y^{T}\dot{\gamma}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">As a result, <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{C:C^{T}Y+Y^{T}C\}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{C:C^{T}Y+Y^{T}C\}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, since the dimension of <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{C:C^{T}Y+Y^{T}C\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{C:C^{T}Y+Y^{T}C\}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="nk-\frac{k(k+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">nk-\frac{k(k+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is easy to check that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{YA,\,A\text{ is a skew-symmetric matrix}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is a skew-symmetric matrix</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{YA,\,A\text{ is a skew-symmetric matrix}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{(1-YY^{T})B,B\text{ is arbitrary }n\times k\text{ matrix}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is arbitrary </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> matrix</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{(1-YY^{T})B,B\text{ is arbitrary }n\times k\text{ matrix}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">are two subspaces of <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>. It is clear that <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(1-YY^{T})B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(1-YY^{T})B\}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-k)k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-k)k</annotation></semantics></math> degrees of freedom, <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{YA\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{YA\}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{k(k-1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{k(k-1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> degrees of freedom and they are orthogonal. Hence we complete the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="ThmProperty2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmProperty2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 2</span></span><span id="ThmProperty2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Normal space of <math id="ThmProperty2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="ThmProperty2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmProperty2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmProperty2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="ThmProperty2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{YA,\,A\text{ is a symmetric }k\times k\text{ matrix}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> is a symmetric </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> matrix</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\{YA,\,A\text{ is a symmetric }k\times k\text{ matrix}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="ThmProperty2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where <math id="ThmProperty2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span>: It is easy to check that</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\{YA,\,A\text{ is a symmetric }k\times k\text{ matrix}\}\perp T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is a symmetric </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> matrix</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\{YA,\,A\text{ is a symmetric }k\times k\text{ matrix}\}\perp T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Note that the dimension of <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\frac{k(k+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})=\frac{k(k+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we complete the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">By these properties, it is easy to check that the projection of a matrix <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in M_{n\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in M_{n\times k}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{Y}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{N}(Z,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{N}(Z,Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Y\frac{Y^{T}Z+Z^{T}Y}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Y\frac{Y^{T}Z+Z^{T}Y}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{T}(Z,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{T}(Z,Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=Y\frac{Y^{T}Z-Z^{T}Y}{2}+(1-YY^{T})Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=Y\frac{Y^{T}Z-Z^{T}Y}{2}+(1-YY^{T})Z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="ThmProperty3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Property">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmProperty3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Property 3</span></span><span id="ThmProperty3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Geodesics of <math id="ThmProperty3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="ThmProperty3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmProperty3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm Exp}:T\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})\to\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm Exp}:T\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})\to\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm Exp}{(x,v)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm Exp}{(x,v)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(x,\,v)\exp\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;-S(0)\\
I&amp;A\end{pmatrix}I_{2p,p}e^{-At}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(x,\,v)\exp\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;-S(0)\\
I&amp;A\end{pmatrix}I_{2p,p}e^{-At}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="ThmProperty3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmProperty3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n}),\,v\in T_{x}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n}),\,v\in T_{x}\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=x^{T}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=x^{T}v</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{2p,p}=\begin{pmatrix}I_{p}\\
0\end{pmatrix}_{2p\times p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{2p,p}=\begin{pmatrix}I_{p}\\
0\end{pmatrix}_{2p\times p}</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp{(Y)}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{Y^{i}}{i!}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp{(Y)}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\frac{Y^{i}}{i!}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="ThmProperty3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmProperty3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. By <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Exp}(x,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Exp}(x,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive the geodesics of Stiefel manifold, and obtain interpolation between two reasonable points on <math id="ThmProperty3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span>: By definition, any geodesics <math id="A1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝕍</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{V}_{k}(\mathbb{R}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\gamma(t)=I_{k\times k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\gamma(t)=I_{k\times k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">By taking derivatives twice, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\ddot{\gamma}(t)+2\dot{\gamma(t)}^{T}\dot{\gamma(t)}+\ddot{\gamma}(t)^{T}\gamma(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(t)^{T}\ddot{\gamma}(t)+2\dot{\gamma(t)}^{T}\dot{\gamma(t)}+\ddot{\gamma}(t)^{T}\gamma(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is geodesic, <math id="A1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\gamma}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\gamma}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> must be in normal space of <math id="A1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ddot{\gamma}(t)+\gamma(t)S=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ddot{\gamma}(t)+\gamma(t)S=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.4" class="ltx_p">Combine this two equation we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ddot{\gamma}(t)+\gamma(\dot{\gamma}^{T}\dot{\gamma})=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ddot{\gamma}(t)+\gamma(\dot{\gamma}^{T}\dot{\gamma})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.5" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t)=\gamma^{T}\gamma,\quad A(t)=\gamma^{T}\dot{\gamma}\quad S=\dot{\gamma}^{T}\dot{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>γ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t)=\gamma^{T}\gamma,\quad A(t)=\gamma^{T}\dot{\gamma}\quad S=\dot{\gamma}^{T}\dot{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.6" class="ltx_p">By Equation <a href="#A1.E1" title="In Appendix A Key Properties of Stiefel Manifold 𝕍_𝑘⁢(ℝ^𝑛) ‣ Graph Generation with Spectral Geodesic Flow Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{C}=A^{T}+A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{C}=A^{T}+A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{A}=-CS+S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{A}=-CS+S</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{S}=[A,S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{S}=[A,S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.7" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[A,S]=AS-SA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[A,S]=AS-SA</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is skew-symmetric, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C=I</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A=A(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A=A(0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S=e^{At}S(0)e^{-At}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S=e^{At}S(0)e^{-At}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.8" class="ltx_p">By these equations, we know that:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}(Ye^{At},\dot{Y}e^{At})=(Ye^{At},\dot{Y}e^{At})\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;-S(0)\\
I&amp;A\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>A</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}(Ye^{At},\dot{Y}e^{At})=(Ye^{At},\dot{Y}e^{At})\begin{pmatrix}A&amp;-S(0)\\
I&amp;A\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p7.9" class="ltx_p">By integration, we complete the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hfill\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hfill\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Geodesics and the conditional vector field</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid introducing complex concepts, here we provide an intuitive understanding to the property used in section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="IV-A Conditional Flow Mapping Design ‣ IV Method ‣ Graph Generation with Spectral Geodesic Flow Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-A</span></a>. Define the geodesic interpolation as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})=x_{t}:={\rm Exp}{\big(U_{0},t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})=x_{t}:={\rm Exp}{\big(U_{0},t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Its corresponding conditional vector field is given by:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle u_{t}(\cdot|U_{1})=\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})={\rm Log}{(U_{t},U_{1})}\frac{\|{\rm Log}{(U_{0},U_{1})}\|}{\|{\rm Log}{(U_{t},U_{1})}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{t}(\cdot|U_{1})=\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})={\rm Log}{(U_{t},U_{1})}\frac{\|{\rm Log}{(U_{0},U_{1})}\|}{\|{\rm Log}{(U_{t},U_{1})}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intuitive Explanation:</span> When everything is well-defined, <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Exp}{\big(U_{0},t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Exp}{\big(U_{0},t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-quantile on the shortest path connecting <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> (the point on the shortest path where the distance from <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to this point, divided by the total distance from <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, equals <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>). A particle moving along this path exhibits the following property: Starting from <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and moving along the shortest path towards <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, if the particle first travels a distance <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to reach <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then moves along the shortest path from <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> for a distance <math id="A2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the resulting position <math id="A2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t_{0}+\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t_{0}+\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math> will be the same as if it had traveled the total distance <math id="A2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}+d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}+d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> directly along the path. Therefore, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi_{t_{0}+\Delta t}(U_{0}|U_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi_{t_{0}+\Delta t}(U_{0}|U_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\rm Exp}\!\left(U_{0},(t_{0}+\Delta t)\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.700em;" width="1.700em"><mi>Exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\rm Exp}\!\left(U_{0},(t_{0}+\Delta t)\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\rm Exp}\!\left(x_{t_{0}},d_{1}\cdot\frac{{\rm Log}(U_{t_{0}},U_{1})}{\lVert{\rm Log}(U_{t_{0}},U_{1})\rVert}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.700em;" width="1.700em"><mi>Exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\rm Exp}\!\left(x_{t_{0}},d_{1}\cdot\frac{{\rm Log}(U_{t_{0}},U_{1})}{\lVert{\rm Log}(U_{t_{0}},U_{1})\rVert}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\Delta t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)\|=d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta t\cdot{\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})\big)\|=d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle v_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle v_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:={\rm Log}(U_{t},U_{1}),\quad v_{0}:={\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:={\rm Log}(U_{t},U_{1}),\quad v_{0}:={\rm Log}(U_{0},U_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\psi_{t}(U_{0}|U_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{{\rm Exp}\big(x_{t},d_{1}\cdot\frac{v_{t}}{\|v_{t}\|}\big)-x_{t}}{\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{{\rm Exp}\big(x_{t},d_{1}\cdot\frac{v_{t}}{\|v_{t}\|}\big)-x_{t}}{\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{{\rm Exp}\big(x_{t},\Delta t\cdot\|v_{0}\|\cdot\frac{v_{t}}{\|v_{t}\|}\big)-x_{t}}{\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\Delta t\to 0}\frac{{\rm Exp}\big(x_{t},\Delta t\cdot\|v_{0}\|\cdot\frac{v_{t}}{\|v_{t}\|}\big)-x_{t}}{\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\rm Log}(U_{t},U_{1})\frac{\|v_{0}\|}{\|v_{t}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\rm Log}(U_{t},U_{1})\frac{\|v_{0}\|}{\|v_{t}\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<figure id="A3.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE IX: </span>Architecture details of eigenvalue generator.</figcaption>
<div id="A3.T9.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:56.7pt;vertical-align:-26.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-125.7pt,20.7pt) scale(0.57838686743541,0.57838686743541) ;">
<table id="A3.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T9.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"></th>
<th id="A3.T9.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Hyperparameter</th>
<td id="A3.T9.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Ego-small</td>
<td id="A3.T9.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Community-small</td>
<td id="A3.T9.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Planar</td>
